.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
A MultiList (and an Ext18List, its older name) displays its rows in a
child widget of the private class \fBXmI18List\fP\&. These functions
operate on that child, not on the MultiList, and are exported only
because the MultiList calls them from another file\&. They are not part
of the supported interface: \fB<Xm/MultiListP\&.h>\fP declares only
\fBXmI18ListGetSelectedRows\fP, \fBXmI18ListToggleRow\fP and the two
\fBXm18IList\fP functions, and none of them checks the class of its
widget argument\&. Applications should call the MultiList function
listed below instead, which takes the MultiList widget, locks the
application context and passes the request on:
.PP
.TS
tab(;);
lB lB
l l.
Internal function;Use instead
_
XmI18ListGetSelectedRows;\fBXmMultiListGetSelectedRows\fP(3)
XmI18ListGetSelectedRowArray;\fBXmMultiListGetSelectedRowArray\fP(3)
XmI18ListSelectItems;\fBXmMultiListSelectItems\fP(3)
XmI18ListDeselectItems;\fBXmMultiListDeselectItems\fP(3)
XmI18ListSelectAllItems;\fBXmMultiListSelectAllItems\fP(3)
XmI18ListSelectRow;\fBXmMultiListSelectRow\fP(3)
XmI18ListDeselectRow;\fBXmMultiListDeselectRow\fP(3)
XmI18ListToggleRow;\fBXmMultiListToggleRow\fP(3)
XmI18ListMakeRowVisible;\fBXmMultiListMakeRowVisible\fP(3)
Xm18IListUnselectItem;\fBXmMultiListUnselectItem\fP(3)
Xm18IListUnselectAllItems;\fBXmMultiListUnselectAllItems\fP(3)
.TE
.PP
Each of these behaves as described on the page of its MultiList
counterpart\&.
.PP
\fBXmI18ListDoSearch\fP and \fBXmI18ListFindRow\fP implement the find
button of the MultiList (\fBXmNshowFind\fP)\&. Both search the cells
of the list, starting at the first selected row (or the first row), for
\fIstr\fP\&. When \fIreset\fP is True the search starts again at the
first column; otherwise it continues after the column where the
previous search stopped\&. \fBXmI18ListDoSearch\fP selects the row it
finds and scrolls the matching cell into view\&.
\fBXmI18ListFindRow\fP stores the column of the match in
\fI*found_column\fP and does the same only when \fIdo_visual\fP is
True\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
\fBXmI18ListDoSearch\fP returns True if a match was found\&.
\fBXmI18ListFindRow\fP returns the row of the match, or NULL\&. The
other functions return what their MultiList counterparts return\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fBXmMultiList\fP(3) and \fBXmExt18List\fP(3)\&.
